# EYEPRINTS — THE UNLOCK ENGINE

This is the public, **synthetic-only** EYEPRINTS browser module integrated into TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY. Launch [the local static app](./index.html), or access it from the factory ecosystem catalog. The more comprehensive Python/OpenCV v1.1 local research package is a separate working artifact that still needs committed source files and a deployment pipeline before it can run as a hosted backend.

## Included

- Synthetic eye generator, interactive Wadjet overlay, six binary fractions and symbolic remainder
- Eye-width/inter-eye distance illustration (not biometric identity evidence)
- Five foundational ancient vocabulary entries; fictional cosmic overlays marked explicitly
- LASIK, PRK/ASA, SMILE, EVO ICL, and experimental EMR procedure descriptions
- Optional non-biometric JSON export; no webcam, backend, uploads, authentication, identity storage or health conclusions

## Remaining integration gates

1. Vendor and audit the Python/OpenCV source into this directory after code/security review.
2. Ship only behind a protected local or appropriately hardened service; never expose raw eye images or biometric templates through the public static page.
3. Run accuracy, PAD, accessibility, performance and privacy evaluations before offering any security use.
4. Do not gate user authorization on Pythagorean geometry, historical terms, Wadjet ratios, synthetic scores or color reflectance.
5. The 35-entry lexical research dataset in the local application is draft content; review original scripts and historical citations before publishing it as verified scholarship.

Product: ONE — The Last App / TABOR ROOT / TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY. Author: Nathan Tabor.
